---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Figure from '../../components/Figure.astro';
import { withBase } from '../../lib/github';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Sweeps & results"
  description="Parameter sweeps and reading Semper result fields."
  path="/manual/sweeps-results"
>
  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 3rem">
    <p class="crumb">
      <a href={withBase('/manual')}>← Manual</a>
    </p>
    <h2>Sweeps &amp; results</h2>
    <p class="sub">Why to sweep, how to read the lattice, and how to inspect field maps.</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h3>Why sweep</h3>
      <p>
        Strain is computed from displacement, so it depends on how much you smooth. A small virtual
        strain gauge (VSG) keeps peaks but adds noise; a large VSG smooths peaks. A
        <strong>sweep</strong> solves one deformed frame across many subset × window combinations so
        you can see where the answer stops changing.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="lead-label">Why it matters:</span> good DIC practice asks you to show that
        reported strain is not an accident of one VSG choice.
      </p>

      <h3>Setting up a sweep</h3>
      <p><span class="lead-label">In the app:</span> on step 3, set ranges and sample counts.</p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Control</th>
            <th>Range</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Subset range</td>
            <td>15–121, odd</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Strain window range</td>
            <td>5–101, odd</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Step denominator</td>
            <td>2–9 (step = subset ÷ n, never below 1 px)</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Samples per axis</td>
            <td>1–8 (runtime is the product)</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>Start at 3 × 3. Look for the VSG where the curves stop separating.</p>
      <Figure
        src="/manual/vsg.svg"
        alt="VSG formula diagram"
        caption="Each lattice node reports its VSG. Quote that number with your strain maps."
      />

      <h3>Result lattice</h3>
      <Figure
        src="/manual/lattice.svg"
        alt="Lattice of filled and hollow result nodes"
        caption="Filled dots solved; hollow rings were skipped — tap a hollow node for the reason."
      />
      <ul>
        <li>Tap — highlight that curve</li>
        <li>Double-tap or long-press — open that result</li>
        <li>Exx / Eyy / Exy — switch strain component</li>
      </ul>

      <h3>Reading results</h3>
      <Figure
        src="/manual/ui-viewer.svg"
        alt="Schematic result viewer with field tabs and Inspect tools"
        caption="Field tabs along the top; Inspect, X/Y, and Max/Min below the map."
        phone
      />
      <p>
        Pinch to zoom, drag to pan. The strip under the image shows max, mean, and min.
      </p>
      <p>
        <span class="lead-label">In the app:</span> colour scale defaults to Auto — each frame
        rescales alone, so frames are not comparable by eye. Set fixed min/max, or use the summary
        animation (one scale for the whole sequence).
      </p>
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Tool</th>
            <th>Does</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr>
            <td>Inspect</td>
            <td>Probe location and value under your finger</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>X, Y</td>
            <td>Jump the probe to typed coordinates</td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td>Max/Min</td>
            <td>Mark extrema with values and positions</td>
          </tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p>
        The ⓘ <strong>Settings used</strong> sheet is provenance. Changing settings later never
        rewrites an old result.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="cta-row" style="margin-top: 1.5rem">
      <a class="btn btn-primary" href={withBase('/manual/exports-manage')}>Open Exports</a>
      <a class="btn btn-ghost" href={withBase('/manual/analysis')}>Back</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
